Who We Are

Verve has created a more efficient and privacy-focused way to buy and monetize advertising. Verve is an ecosystem of demand and supply technologies fusing data, media, and technology together to deliver results and growth to both advertisers and publishers-no matter the screen or location, no matter who, what, or where a customer is. With offices across the globe and with an eye on servicing forward-thinking advertising customers, Verve’s solutions are trusted by more than 90 of the United States’ top 100 advertisers, 4,000 publishers globally, and the world’s top demand-side platforms. Learn more at verve.com .

Who You Are

This is a high-visibility player-manager role for an ambitious Big 4 professional ready to make the move into industry. Based in Dublin and reporting to the VP of Finance, you will lead and drive the group's compliance agenda and own the delivery of our PCAOB audits.

You will combine hands-on technical work with leading a small team, and act as a trusted adviser to the VP of Finance and other senior finance leaders. It is a chance to build the audit and compliance framework of a fast-growing international business, with real influence from day one.

What You Will Do

• Lead the end-to-end PCAOB audit process: plan timelines, coordinate requests, prepare supporting schedules and act as the main day-to-day contact for the external auditors.&nbsp;

• Drive timely resolution of audit findings, management letter points and control deficiencies, tracking remediation through to close.&nbsp;

• Own the group finance compliance calendar, covering statutory filings, tax returns and regulatory deadlines across entities, so that nothing is missed.&nbsp;

• Design, document and test internal controls over financial reporting, and continuously strengthen the control environment.&nbsp;

• Prepare and review technical accounting memos and position papers on complex or judgemental areas.&nbsp;

• Support the VP of Finance and other senior finance leaders with analysis, board and audit committee materials, and ad hoc projects.&nbsp;

• Roll up your sleeves as a player-manager, preparing reconciliations, schedules and reviews alongside the team.&nbsp;

• Lead, coach and develop a small team, building audit readiness and compliance discipline across the wider finance function.&nbsp;

• Work cross-functionally with Accounting, Tax, Legal, FP&amp;A and business-unit finance teams to embed best practice.&nbsp;

• Drive process improvements that make audits faster, smoother and less disruptive for the business.

What You Will Bring

• Qualified accountant (ACA, ACCA, CPA or European equivalent).&nbsp;

• Big 4 audit background, ideally at Manager or Senior Manager level.&nbsp;

• Direct experience of PCAOB audits, with a strong understanding of PCAOB standards and US GAAP or IFRS.&nbsp;

• Solid knowledge of internal controls frameworks such as SOX or COSO, including control design and testing.&nbsp;

• Experience leading or supervising audit teams, and the willingness to stay hands-on in a player-manager role.&nbsp;

• Strong technical accounting skills and the ability to write clear, well-reasoned accounting papers.&nbsp;

• Highly organised, with a track record of managing multiple deadlines and stakeholders at once.&nbsp;

• Confident communicator who can challenge constructively and build trust with auditors and senior leaders.&nbsp;

• Advanced Excel skills. Preferred: SAP or Oracle, BlackLine, Workiva or similar tools.

• A continuous-improvement mindset and comfort in a fast-moving, international environment.

